\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The $(\mu ,\nu )$ matrix for one observation face $\lambda $. Diagonal entries (bold) are shared: the metric cannot distinguish the two roots there. Upper-triangle entries belong to the $s = +1$ projection (TetA, retained). Lower-triangle entries belong to the $s = -1$ projection (TetB, discarded by the torsion-free condition). The same pattern repeats for all four values of $\lambda $.}}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:matrix}{{1}{1}{The $(\mu ,\nu )$ matrix for one observation face $\lambda $. Diagonal entries (bold) are shared: the metric cannot distinguish the two roots there. Upper-triangle entries belong to the $s = +1$ projection (TetA, retained). Lower-triangle entries belong to the $s = -1$ projection (TetB, discarded by the torsion-free condition). The same pattern repeats for all four values of $\lambda $}{figure.1}{}}
